===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|fey||fated to die}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fǣġe||doomed to die, timid}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*faigijaz||cowardly, wicked}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*peyk-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*peyg-||ill-meaning, bad}}. Akin to {{cog|osx|fēgi}} whence {{cog|nl|veeg||doomed, near death}}, {{cog|goh|feigi||appointed for death, ungodly}} whence {{cog|de|feige||cowardly}}, {{cog|non|feigr||doomed}} whence the {{cog|is|feigur||doomed to die}}, {{cog|ang|fāh||outlawed, hostile}}. More at {{l|en|foe}}.

